      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T05:40:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Signal handling doesn\u0027t propagate to the child process. The build is launched as command \"$@\" \u0026 wait \"$!\", and TERM/INT/HUP/QUIT traps just call exit. But exiting the parent doesn\u0027t send a signal to the backgrounded child, so on docker stop/timeout the actual build tool (d2) can be left running as an orphan until it finishes on its own. Consider trapping the signal, forwarding it to the child (kill -TERM \"$!\"), then waiting before exiting.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "4ed45b0e995acf84474aa7c5cce43a5168fefab1",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
