      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T22:01:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That depends on what you mean by avoid. You can just add a directory with a dockerfile (and whatever it needs) here instead but that means each presentation will build its own image without central control. We can in theory read a configuration file saying what image is used but that seems somewhat pointless when a symlink carries the intended meaning perfectly. Ultimately I think that symlinks is the best way to do this. I do have protections against symlinks misbehaving inside the realfile function in build-all.sh",
